1
00:00:00,060 --> 00:00:02,580
Hi, I'm Phil from BBC Learning English.

2
00:00:02,580 --> 00:00:04,640
Today, I'm going to tell you how we use

3
00:00:04,640 --> 00:00:09,100
play, do and go with different sports.

4
00:00:09,520 --> 00:00:13,820
So, for team sports or ball games, we use play.

5
00:00:13,820 --> 00:00:14,760
So, I can say:

6
00:00:14,760 --> 00:00:17,900
I play football. I don't play tennis.

7
00:00:18,060 --> 00:00:20,920
For more individual activities, we use do.

8
00:00:20,920 --> 00:00:21,620
So, we can say:

9
00:00:21,620 --> 00:00:24,560
I do exercise. I don't do judo.

10
00:00:25,180 --> 00:00:31,000
Then, for activities ending in –ING, we often use go.

11
00:00:31,000 --> 00:00:31,860
So, I can say:

12
00:00:31,860 --> 00:00:33,360
I go running.

13
00:00:33,360 --> 00:00:33,860
Or:

14
00:00:33,860 --> 00:00:35,780
I don't go swimming.

15
00:00:35,860 --> 00:00:38,100
Of course, there are some exceptions,

16
00:00:38,100 --> 00:00:39,860
but try to remember.

17
00:00:39,860 --> 00:00:42,430
Play for team sports or ball games.

18
00:00:42,700 --> 00:00:45,500
Do for individual activities

19
00:00:45,500 --> 00:00:49,840
and go for activities ending in –ING.

